# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

*_output/

*.v
# Committed Rocq `.v` goldens live here; `*.v` above still ignores compiler output.
!/tests/test_data/rocq/*.v
# The vendored Rocq stub sources are code, not compiler output. Without this
# negation a new stub file is silently skipped by `git add` (the pre-existing
# stub files were only ever tracked via a historical force-add).
!/core/wasm-to-v/rocq-stub/**/*.v

# Rocq build outputs. `coqc` writes them next to the source it compiles, so
# building the vendored stub in place — or checking an emitted `.v` beside a
# committed golden — drops them straight into a tracked directory. The forms
# Rocq dot-prefixes (`.<module>.aux`, `.lia.cache`, and a `.coq-native/`
# directory under native compilation) are already caught by the blanket `.*`
# rule below; the two spellable here are named anyway so the artifact set stays
# readable in one place and survives any narrowing of that rule.
*.vo
*.vok
*.vos
*.glob
*.aux
.lia.cache

out
test_data/**/*.json

# Local end-to-end linker scratchpad (kept locally, never committed)
scratch/

# Coverage reports
lcov.info
*.profraw
*.profdata
coverage/
cobertura.xml

.*
!.github/workflows/
!.cargo/
!.gitattributes

external/
/*.md
!README.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!CHANGELOG.md
*.vsix
editors/vscode/package-lock.json
editors/vscode/node_modules/

# mdBook render output
/book/book/
/scratch
